# Hexagonal Architecture — Per-Service Layout

Every service under `apps/<service>/src/` follows the same Ports & Adapters layout. The reference implementation is [apps/booking-service/src/app.ts](../../apps/booking-service/src/app.ts).

## Layer Hierarchy (outermost to innermost)

- `entrypoints/http/` — NestJS `@Controller` classes. HTTP adapters.
- `entrypoints/event-consumers/` — Kafka consumer handler classes.
- `domain/use-cases/` — Command interfaces + use case handler classes.
- `domain/entities/` — Aggregate roots, value objects, enums (innermost).
- `infrastructure/database/` — Persistence model interfaces + repository implementations.
- `infrastructure/external-services/` — Third-party adapter classes.
- `config/` — Environment configuration factories.
- `app.ts` — Inline `@Module` definition + `create<Service>Module()` factory.
- `main.ts` — `NestFactory.create` bootstrap.

## Permitted Import Paths

- `entrypoints/http/` may import from `domain/use-cases/`, `domain/entities/`, `@ente-doctor/contracts`.
- `entrypoints/event-consumers/` may import from `domain/use-cases/`, `domain/entities/`, `@ente-doctor/event-bus`.
- `domain/use-cases/` may import from `domain/entities/`, `@ente-doctor/common`, `@ente-doctor/contracts`.
- `domain/entities/` may import from `@ente-doctor/common`, `@ente-doctor/contracts` (shared value types only).
- `infrastructure/database/` may import from `domain/entities/` (entity types only) and `@ente-doctor/common`.
- `infrastructure/external-services/` may import from `domain/entities/`, `@ente-doctor/contracts`, `@ente-doctor/event-bus`.
- `config/` reads only `process.env`. No internal imports.
- `app.ts` may import from `entrypoints/http/` and `config/`.
- `main.ts` may import from `app.ts`, `@nestjs/core`, `@nestjs/config`, `reflect-metadata`.

## Forbidden Import Paths

- **Forbidden:** `domain/` importing from `infrastructure/`, `entrypoints/`, or `app.ts`.
- **Forbidden:** `infrastructure/` importing from `entrypoints/`.
- **Forbidden:** Importing across `apps/<service>` boundaries. Inter-service communication is **exclusively** Kafka events typed by `@ente-doctor/event-bus`.
- **Forbidden:** Importing from any `dist/` path. Always use the `workspace:*` package name or TypeScript path alias.
- **Forbidden:** Hardcoding Kafka topic strings inline — pull every topic from `EventTopics` in `@ente-doctor/event-bus`.

## Module Definition Rule

- **Always** declare the Nest module inline inside `src/app.ts` and export a `create<Service>Module()` factory that returns the module class. Pattern reference: [apps/booking-service/src/app.ts](../../apps/booking-service/src/app.ts).
- **Never** create a `*.module.ts` file. Existence of any such file is a violation.
- **Never** register a controller, repository, adapter, or use case in the `@Module` decorator until its logic is implemented. Stubs stay out of DI.

## Configuration Access

- `process.env` reads are permitted **only** in `config/*.config.ts`.
- All runtime providers must read configuration via `ConfigService` from `@nestjs/config`.
